>All altars that I've found so far I have converted to Odin. Well, except
>those with a priest.  Should I try to convert these or is it bad?  I think
>I can take the priest but when I've killed a priest of a different
>alignment in the past, I'm sure bad things have happened.

Murdering a generated-peaceful human is inadvisable if you are not of
Chaotic alignment.  Rendering them non-human is not murder, and killing
them once they are no longer human is not murder either. I leave you to
consider your stashed equipment for a possible method, should you choose
to follow this path.

I would, incidentally, suggest that you move your primary stash to the
entrance level of Sokoban as soon as reasonably practical. This greatly
reduces the risk of unpleasant mishaps, since at this point you will only
be going to Sokoban to visit your stash.

>Anyhow, so onto my main question I guess:
>
>I know that next I'll meet Jubliex at some point but then after that, all
>I know is that there are loads of mazes ahead.  I've overheard enough talk
>on #nethack to know that there are a whole bunch of things coming up
>involving a book, a vibrating square and so on - and I'm wondering, Does
>Nethack tell you what to do at some point.

There is a personage in the upper reaches of the Dungeons of Doom who
offers advice.  Her major consultations are significantly informative
in these matters, and you certainly have sufficient funds to afford them.

There is one very important thing to remember, which I'm pretty sure
*she* won't tell you: One of the items you need is in the possession
of the most peculiarly tenacious enemy in the game. Prepare yourself
well before slaying him, not so much for your first confrontation with
him as for what you must endure afterwards.
